+# Audit-Beta findings — wave 6, real-analysis-limits
+
+## Continuity checkpoint — A2 item review
+
+- Owned scope: the two A/B pairs in `wave6-real-analysis-limits.pages.json` (65 items total): `limsup-and-subsequential-limits` and `topology-of-r`, with their companion pages.
+- Owned artifacts: this findings file, `wave6-real-analysis-limits.provenance.jsonl`, and `wave6-real-analysis-limits.proof-contracts.json`. No published item edits are authorized before A3.
+- Completed: all governing instructions; manifest and worktree verification; full item, proof-step, and citation read of the limsup pair; source discovery for its standard results; first five topology A-items through `def-limit-point-r`.
+- Confirmed defect: `cex-zero-times-infinity-indeterminate`, step 3.1, calls the third product “converg[ing] to nothing at all,” although it equals `\iota(k+1)` and converges to `+\infty` in the page's extended-real sense. Proposed A3 class (a) repair: say it diverges to `+\infty` (equivalently, converges to `+\infty` in the extended sense). The real-valued nonconvergence in step 2.2 is correct.
+- Nonfatal prose decay to record: both A-page summaries exceed the current two-paragraph summary shape and contain page/corpus count claims; per the brief these are recorded, not chased.
+- Open constraints: finish every topology item and dependency target; settle all 65 statement/proof provenance rows using only HTTP-200 sources; generate and manually audit 53 proof contracts; run strict contract and audit gates.
+- Exact next action: resume at `thm-closure-characterisations-r`, then complete the topology A/B pair in manifest order.

