[L5] Canonical naturals: $\iota(n) > 0$ and invertible for $n \ge 1$, $\iota$ is strictly increasing, $\iota(1) = 1$, and $\iota(n+n') = \iota(n) + \iota(n')$ ([[lem-of-naturals-positive]]).
