cex-unbounded-closed-set-not-compact 3.1 By step 2.1 the set $\mathbb{Z}$ is closed and by step 1.2 it is not bounded, so [L1] denies that it is compact, refuting claim (i) of [A1]; and by step 1.3 the set $(0,1)$ is bounded and not closed, so [L1] denies that it is compact, refuting claim (ii). Neither hypothesis of [L1] is therefore removable. [step 1.2, step 1.3, step 2.1, A1, L1] ∎

