+- Completed: all governing instructions; manifest and worktree verification; full item, proof-step, and citation read of the limsup pair; source discovery for its standard results; first five topology A-items through `def-limit-point-r`.
+- Confirmed defect: `cex-zero-times-infinity-indeterminate`, step 3.1, calls the third product “converg[ing] to nothing at all,” although it equals `\iota(k+1)` and converges to `+\infty` in the page's extended-real sense. Proposed A3 class (a) repair: say it diverges to `+\infty` (equivalently, converges to `+\infty` in the extended sense). The real-valued nonconvergence in step 2.2 is correct.
